    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.8461v1</id>
    <title>A conjecture on the primitive degree of Tensors</title>
    <updated>2013-10-31T11:10:10Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.8461v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1310.8461v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this paper, we prove: Let A be a nonnegative primitive tensor with order m and dimension n. Then its primitive degree R(A)\leq (n-1)^2+1, and the upper bound is sharp. This confirms a conjecture of Shao [7].</summary>
    <category term="math.CO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
